## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current authority. Vimla is messenger-first with one backend for Web and future Desktop/Mobile.

The API is the single consumer backend for all clients. Do not create platform-specific product route forks. Domain outputs must be semantic, not Next/Tauri/Expo navigation. Durable realtime/sync follows #80/#94–#97; PostgreSQL is truth and Redis/WebSocket are delivery/coordination.

# Backend rules

- Keep NestJS controllers thin: parse/validate/authorize/orchestrate only.
- Domain/business rules belong in application/domain services or shared packages.
- Use explicit module boundaries; avoid circular dependencies.
- Use Fastify-compatible APIs; do not assume Express-specific middleware/request behavior.
- API version consumer endpoints under `/v1` unless framework/provider routes require another namespace.
- Return stable normalized error envelopes/codes. Never leak Prisma/Postgres/provider stack traces in production.
- Correlation/request ID must propagate through logs and important domain operations.
- Protect mutating cookie-authenticated endpoints with trusted-origin/CSRF-safe patterns.
- Every owner-scoped query must use authenticated owner identity as part of lookup/authorization.
- Expensive endpoints require explicit rate/concurrency/size/cost controls.
- Configuration must come from validated `@vimla/config`, not scattered `process.env` reads.
